# Mender workspace safety

## Canonical identity

- Repository root must be `/data_drive/dd/mender` (realpath). Do not open via `/home/ajlennon/data_drive/...`, `dd.code-workspace`, or a linked worktree path.
- This checkout is the **only** write-capable tree for Mender/RT1170 work unless Alex explicitly authorizes a named exception.

## Before and after write work

1. Run `./scripts/check-workspace-safety.py` (local mode) at session start.
2. After meaningful progress, run `./scripts/safety-checkpoint.sh "<message>"` so the change is committed and pushed to GitHub.
3. Before handoff/cleanup/session end, run `./scripts/check-workspace-safety.py --handoff` and leave a clean, pushed tree.

## Source tracking rules

- West dependencies live at repo-root `/zephyr/`, `/modules/`, `/bootloader/`, `/.west/` and stay **gitignored**.
- Application modules under `mender-mcu-integration/modules/` are **tracked source**. Never reintroduce an unanchored `modules/` ignore rule.
- Refuse to proceed if `git check-ignore` matches any source under `mender-mcu-integration/` or `scripts/` that should be tracked.
- Secrets (`*-local.conf`, tokens) stay ignored and must never be staged.

## Parallelism ban (default)

- No second write agent, no `/worktree`, no Best-of-N, no cloud write handoff, no shared/symlinked West deps.
- Read-only research subagents are allowed.

## Explicit exception

If Alex requires parallel write work: stop and confirm branch + lifetime; create an isolated West workspace with fresh deps (no shared symlinks); checkpoint and push before handoff; Trash the worktree only after `git status --short --ignored` is clean and the remote commit is verified.
